1
00:00:00,930 --> 00:00:03,590
3,500 planes in the air...

2
00:00:03,590 --> 00:00:04,030
and suddenly,

3
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:06,900
all of America says: nobody takes off.

4
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:08,040
What happened?

5
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:09,350
This is Trend.

6
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:12,950
What is everyone talking about?

7
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:16,560
On Friday, November 13th,

8
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:18,640
just before 4 p.m. Washington time,

9
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:21,890
the Federal Aviation Administration issued a rare order:

10
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:24,010
a nationwide ground stop.

11
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:27,510
No plane takes off from any airport in the United States.

12
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:31,610
The reason? "Intermittent communication outages."

13
00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:35,010
The longest nationwide stop in twenty-five years...

14
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:37,110
since September 11th.

15
00:00:37,690 --> 00:00:38,310
The result?

16
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,260
More than 9,000 flights cancelled,

17
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:43,320
and more than 7,000 delayed.

18
00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:46,040
Millions of travelers slept in airports,

19
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:47,800
right before the weekend.

20
00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:49,800
Why did the story explode?

21
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:53,120
Because nobody knew the cause.

22
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:54,500
And within a few hours,

23
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:55,890
social media filled with theories:

24
00:00:56,310 --> 00:01:00,220
A cyberattack? A glitch in the new AI tool?

25
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:03,300
A silent war? Homeland Security says:

26
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:05,560
no sign of any attack.

27
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:10,540
And no evidence of AI involvement.

28
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:15,250
17 of the 22 air traffic control centers were affected,

29
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:18,710
but none went completely dark.

30
00:01:18,710 --> 00:01:20,640
So what's the truth? On Saturday morning,

31
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:22,000
the Transportation Secretary gave the explanation...

32
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,740
and it was simpler than anyone imagined.

33
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:28,140
A contractor technician doing routine maintenance at a remote site:

34
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:30,980
replacing decades-old copper wires

35
00:01:31,670 --> 00:01:32,880
with fiber optics,

36
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:35,290
and installing a new router.

37
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:37,350
That small device...

38
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:40,420
started flooding the entire network with requests.

39
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:43,960
A thousand login attempts every four seconds.

40
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:48,260
The system linking control towers across the country choked.

41
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:52,570
The Secretary said: "When I say we're using old equipment...

42
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:55,310
we really are using old equipment." He was asked:

43
00:01:56,760 --> 00:02:00,440
why is this work done at 3 p.m.,

44
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:03,180
and not in the middle of the night?

45
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:04,710
He answered:

46
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:06,640
we'll review the timing.

47
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:07,410
The investigation continues:

48
00:02:08,130 --> 00:02:09,580
human error... or a faulty device?

49
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,880
The most powerful country in the world,

50
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,230
its entire sky stopped...

51
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:14,550
because of a copper wire and a router.

52
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:16,460
So is the problem the device...

53
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:19,190
or those who wait for disaster before upgrading?

54
00:02:21,110 --> 00:02:22,470
Tell me what you think in the comments.

55
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:25,020
Full sources in the video description.

56
